cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, data splits or the FedRevoke audit protocol, please cite the paper below."
title: "FedRevoke: Shadow-Aware Retrieval-Level Forgetting for Cross-Silo Federated Retrieval-Augmented Generation"
abstract: >-
  FedRevoke is a training-free framework for cross-silo retrieval-level
  forgetting in federated retrieval-augmented generation. It turns an
  authenticated revocation request into a provenance-resolved seed set, expands
  it into a two-channel semantic-shadow closure, erases the closure in cascade,
  repairs the ANN index locally without retraining, and records the outcome in a
  hash-chained deletion log.
type: software
license: MIT
